    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432-a2">

                <pb facs="0757" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg687"/>

                <head>Mr. Dickinson to Señor Cortez</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Leon</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-01-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 8, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Your esteemed note of December 27
                    is received, and it is with profound satisfaction that I learn from it that the
                    present able and vigilant chief magistrate of this republic has again suppressed
                    the vain attempt to subvert his government.</p>
                <p>I forward by this mail the agreeable news to my government, and sincerely hope
                    that a long and happy peace may be in store for this republic.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. B. DICKINSON.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rosalio Cortez, Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs, &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
